# L §5.16 The closed list: a dist fact's distribution is one the list holds, and "A distribution the list doesn't hold
# is written from one it does" (a draw by lot, e[discrete(...)]); in a dist def's rule d1 is the distribution (it is
# not sampled there), and no arithmetic makes a distribution value: d1 + sh is refused at load (L §8.4 What isn't
# defined is refused; LOAD-UNIT, a type error). (Writer 8: was REFCORE-NOT-YET.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input mu: money PLN
input sd: money PLN
input sh: money PLN
def d1: dist PLN = normal(mu, sd) to 0.01 PLN
def d2: dist PLN = d1 + sh

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  mu = 10.00 PLN
  sd = 2.00 PLN
  sh = 1.00 PLN

ask q: mean(d2)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT dist PLN and money PLN in arithmetic: a distribution value is no number ...
